3608:# --- PLAN-164 W1 (ADR-110-AMEND-1) — pair-rail registration-timeout VALUE
3609:# --- migration. WHY: the harness kills a hook at its settings.json
3610:# --- registration timeout, and the pre-PLAN-164 cap (60s) sat BELOW the
3611:# --- measured codex verdict latency (p95 ~75s under load; 12/12 historical
3612:# --- pair_rail_case rows were F/TIMEOUT — PLAN-163/probes/
3613:# --- GATE-V2-2026-07-29-FAIL-diagnosis.md). Ratified semantics
3614:# --- (OQ2=150, recalibrated to 210 by ADR-110-AMEND-2): bump the
3615:# --- check_pair_rail.py PreToolUse registration timeout IFF the current
3616:# --- value is one of the SUPERSEDED SHIPPED caps; ANY other
3617:# --- adopter-chosen value is PRESERVED (named WARN); already-at-target is
3618:# --- a no-op; an entry with NO timeout key is left untouched (harness
3619:# --- default, not an adopter choice of an old cap). The NEW cap is
3620:# --- DERIVED from the template artifact
3621:# --- (settings.base.json pair-rail entry — install.sh copies it verbatim,
3622:# --- so template value == post-install value == migration target); each
3623:# --- OLD cap is a frozen historical literal (none exists in any live
3624:# --- artifact once this migration lands), exactly like the "old" column of
3625:# --- the T5.4 table above. Fail-open: an unreadable template or a
3626:# --- non-unique/non-int template cap skips ONLY this leaf (stderr NOTE) —
3627:# --- the rest of the migration is unaffected.
3628:# ADR-110-AMEND-2: the set of SUPERSEDED SHIPPED defaults, not a single
3629:# literal. 60 was the pre-PLAN-164 cap; 150 was the PLAN-164/AMEND-1 cap
3630:# shipped in v1.2.0 and superseded by the AMEND-2 value 210. A v1.2.0
3631:# adopter sits at exactly 150, and leaving it there is NOT conservative:
3632:# with the hook-internal default now 180, a 150s registration lets the
3633:# HARNESS kill the hook BEFORE the internal codex cap fires -- and a
3634:# killed hook emits NO pair_rail_case at all (AMEND-2 section 6:
3635:# fail-open with no event, invisible to the instrument in both numerator
3636:# and denominator). That is strictly worse than the case F it replaces,
3637:# so a shipped default must keep migrating. Every member is a frozen
3638:# historical literal that no longer exists in any live artifact; an
3639:# adopter value outside this set is a genuine choice and stays PRESERVED
3640:# + WARNED.
3641:# NOTE: this whole block is a bash SINGLE-QUOTED -c string. No apostrophe
3642:# may appear anywhere in it -- one terminates the string and silently
3643:# turns the migration into a no-op (the tests then read the seeded value
3644:# back unchanged, which looks like a logic bug, not a quoting bug).
3645:OLD_PAIR_RAIL_CAPS = (60, 150)
