4339:# ===========================================================================
4340:# PLAN-183 W5 (D1) — deliver the docs/ + .github/ trees install.sh has always
4341:# shipped and this script never did.
4342:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
4343:# MEASURED (S323, re-run S327): `grep -c github scripts/upgrade.sh` = 0 and
4344:# every `docs` hit was a comment. install.sh delivers both trees through
4345:# install_docs_templates (:1533) and install_github_templates (:1580); nothing
4346:# here ever did. That is defect D1, and it is what holds the parity e2e at
4347:# STALE 3 (measured baseline: docs/BRANCH-PROTECTION.md,
4348:# .github/workflows/validate.yml.template, .github/workflows/benchmarks.yml.template).
4349:#
4350:# THE ROUTE TABLE IS THE TRUTH. Destination -> source is answered ONLY by
4351:# scripts/delivery-routes.tsv, through the SAME reader the manifest generator
4352:# uses (_wbm_route_src / _wbm_route_dests, D3). A second destination list here
4353:# would be the "local branch that decides ownership" CLAUDE.md §4 forbids and
4354:# this repo has already paid for twice (PLAN-182: 16 modules -> one resolver;
4355:# PLAN-167: _ownership_verdict).
4356:#
4357:# OWNERSHIP LADDER — the whole point is to REFRESH framework bytes without
4358:# ever taking an adopter's file. Per destination, in order:
4359:#   absent                                    -> INSTALLED
4360:#   target == current framework source        -> IDENTICAL   (no write)
4361:#   target == the digest the BASELINE MANIFEST recorded for it
4362:#                                             -> REFRESHED (prior record)
4363:#   target == some PRIOR GENERATION of the source in $SOURCE_DIR's git history
4364:#                                             -> REFRESHED (pristine prior generation)
4365:#   anything else                             -> PRESERVED (loud, never written)
4366:# Rungs 3 and 4 are both already-established mechanisms here: ownership
4367:# continuity by recorded digest (install.sh:2504's HASH_PRIOR_RECORD shape)
4368:# and the hash-gated generation refresh of _refresh_schema_doc (:3204-3212).
4369:# Neither is a heuristic about content; both are evidence that the framework
4370:# put those exact bytes there. When SOURCE_DIR is not a git checkout (a
4371:# release tarball) rung 4 yields nothing and the verdict falls to PRESERVED —
4372:# under-claiming, which is the recoverable direction.
4373:#
4374:# The generations are DERIVED FROM GIT at run time, never from tags and never
4375:# from a hand-maintained pin list. _refresh_schema_doc's hardcoded pins carry
4376:# a standing contract ("every commit that changes the doc must append the
4377:# replaced generation's hash") that has already been violated once in this
4378:# repo (S313, the 996d72b red). Deriving removes the contract instead of
4379:# adding five more of them.
4380:#
4381:# TWO-STAGE docs/ ROUTE (§9.7 item 1): install.sh cp's the docs templates and
4382:# THEN rewrites them in place through apply_placeholder_substitutions
4383:# (:2226-2231). Both templates carry ZERO {{...}} markers today (measured), so
4384:# the post-substitution bytes equal the template bytes and comparing against
4385:# the template is correct. That is an ACCIDENT of content, not a design
4386:# guarantee: the moment a marker appears in either file the comparison starts
4387:# lying. The guard for that is the parity e2e, which compares the DELIVERED
4388:# trees and would go red the same day. .github/ is NOT in the substitution
4389:# walk (explicit_files, install.sh:2196-2214) and is verbatim by construction.
4390:# ===========================================================================
4391:echo ""
4392:echo "==> Delivering docs/ + .github/ framework templates (PLAN-183 W5 D1)"
4393:
4394:_UP_TPL_ROUTES=0
4395:_UP_TPL_ROWS=0          # rail round-1 F2: the table's raw data-row count
4396:_UP_TPL_INSTALLED=0
4397:_UP_TPL_REFRESHED=0
4398:_UP_TPL_IDENTICAL=0
4399:_UP_TPL_PRESERVED=0
4400:_UP_TPL_SKIPPED=0
4401:_D1_DELIVERY_RAN=0
4402:_D1_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES=""
4403:_D1_CODEOWNERS_REGISTERED=0
4404:# rail round-2 F2 (second half) — a FAILED precondition must reach the CALLER.
4405:# Pre-cure, both precondition branches below printed an ERROR and the upgrade
4406:# still exited 0: docs/ and .github/ undelivered, `echo $?` saying success.
4407:# DEFERRED, not an immediate `exit`: this block sits ~500 lines before the end
4408:# and the mis-install purge scan, the C.7 baseline-manifest rewrite and
4409:# _write_upgrade_state all still have to run — aborting here would leave the
4410:# target HALF-upgraded, which is strictly worse than the fail-open being
4411:# cured. So the rest of the upgrade completes, the summary line carries
4412:# `precondition=FAILED` for log-only consumers, and the process exits 3.
4413:_UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_FAILED=0
4414:# rail round-3 F2 — WHICH precondition failed, in one machine-readable token.
4415:# The deferred exit and the banner are both derived from the flag above; this
4416:# is what makes the PERSISTED record say more than "not true": a durable audit
4417:# entry that only knows "failed" cannot be triaged a week later.
4418:_UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_REASON=""
4419:
4420:# rc.1 re-pass part 1 P1-4 — a route the table DECLARES and this run cannot
4421:# render is a FAILED delivery, never "nothing to do". Pre-cure the four sites
4422:# that call this printed a named SKIP, bumped _UP_TPL_SKIPPED, satisfied the
4423:# conservation law, and left the flag at 0: "Upgrade complete." and exit 0 with
4424:# docs/ or .github/ NOT delivered — the exact observable CHANGELOG.md:48 of
4425:# this release denies ("A failed delivery exits 3 and persists
4426:# upgrade_succeeded: false"), and the same shape as the D1..D4 class that cost
4427:# six sessions of red main. The two OTHER ways to poison the same table (zero
4428:# routes, a rejected row) already exit 3; this one did not, and that
4429:# inconsistency was the finding.
4430:# One function, not four inline pairs: the sites that must fail-closed are a
4431:# CLASS, and a fifth one added later either calls this or is visibly missing it.
4432:# The SKIPPED counter stays where it was — a refusal is still a verdict, so the
4433:# conservation law below keeps holding and the summary line still balances.
4434:# NOT called from the BENIGN skips, which are decisions rather than failures:
4435:# "branch not taken" (the mutually exclusive CODEOWNERS/.template pair),
4436:# "CODEOWNERS present"/"present as symlink" (the same exclusivity), and
4437:# "source missing (at pin ...)" (a --pin tree legitimately lacking the bytes).
4438:_up_route_unrenderable() {
4439:  _UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_FAILED=1
4440:  _UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_REASON="unrenderable-transform"
4441:}
4442:
4443:# sha256 of every generation of a SOURCE relpath in $SOURCE_DIR's git history,
4444:# one per line, deduplicated. $2 (optional) is a validated OWNER_HANDLE: when
4445:# non-empty each generation is RENDERED through the same substitution
4446:# install.sh applies before hashing, so the comparison happens on the bytes
4447:# that were actually DELIVERED, never on the unrendered template.
4448:# Empty output whenever the evidence cannot be produced (no git, no hasher,
4449:# SOURCE_DIR is not a checkout, path unknown to history) — the caller then has
4450:# no prior-generation evidence and PRESERVES.
4451:_up_tpl_generations() {
4452:  _utg_rel="$1"
4453:  _utg_handle="${2:-}"
4454:  _utg_out=""
4455:  command -v git >/dev/null 2>&1 || { printf ''; return 0; }
4456:  command -v _hash_stdin >/dev/null 2>&1 || { printf ''; return 0; }
4457:  git -C "$SOURCE_DIR" rev-parse --git-dir >/dev/null 2>&1 || { printf ''; return 0; }
4458:  while IFS= read -r _utg_commit; do
4459:    [ -n "$_utg_commit" ] || continue
4460:    _utg_blob="$( git -C "$SOURCE_DIR" rev-parse "$_utg_commit:$_utg_rel" 2>/dev/null || true )"
4461:    [ -n "$_utg_blob" ] || continue
4462:    if [ -n "$_utg_handle" ]; then
4463:      _utg_hash="$( git -C "$SOURCE_DIR" cat-file blob "$_utg_blob" 2>/dev/null \
4464:                    | sed "s/{{OWNER_HANDLE}}/$_utg_handle/g" \
4465:                    | _hash_stdin 2>/dev/null || true )"
4466:    else
4467:      _utg_hash="$( git -C "$SOURCE_DIR" cat-file blob "$_utg_blob" 2>/dev/null \
4468:                    | _hash_stdin 2>/dev/null || true )"
4469:    fi
4470:    [ -n "$_utg_hash" ] || continue
4471:    case "
4472:$_utg_out" in
4473:      *"
4474:$_utg_hash
4475:"*) continue ;;
4476:    esac
4477:    _utg_out="$_utg_out$_utg_hash
4478:"
4479:  done < <( git -C "$SOURCE_DIR" log --format='%H' -- "$_utg_rel" 2>/dev/null || true )
4480:  printf '%s' "$_utg_out"
4481:}
4482:
4483:# Refuse to write through a symlinked LEAF or any symlinked ANCESTOR. Verbatim
4484:# posture of _refresh_schema_doc (:3236-3255) and NOT optional here: a dangling
4485:# link makes `cp` materialise its referent OUTSIDE $TARGET, which PLAN-183
4486:# §9.1 reproduced as a live install.sh defect (PLAN-185 F1). upgrade.sh does
4487:# not get to ship the same hole on a new route. Returns 0 when the write must
4488:# be refused.
4489:_up_tpl_symlink_refuses() {
4490:  _uts_rel="$1"
4491:  if [ -L "$TARGET/$_uts_rel" ]; then
4492:    echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED $_uts_rel (destination is a symlink — a refresh would write through it, outside the target; replace the link manually if that is intended)"
4493:    return 0
4494:  fi
4495:  _uts_walk="$( dirname "$_uts_rel" )"
4496:  while [ -n "$_uts_walk" ] && [ "$_uts_walk" != "." ] && [ "$_uts_walk" != "/" ]; do
4497:    if [ -L "$TARGET/$_uts_walk" ]; then
4498:      echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED $_uts_rel (ancestor $_uts_walk is a symlink — refusing to write through it)"
4499:      return 0
4500:    fi
4501:    _uts_walk="$( dirname "$_uts_walk" )"
4502:  done
4503:  return 1
4504:}
4505:
4506:# Write the delivered bytes by the SAME mechanism install.sh uses for that
4507:# route, because the MECHANISM decides the resulting file MODE and MODE_DIFF
4508:# is a FATAL class in the very parity gate this wave exists to turn green.
4509:#   identity route : `cp` — exactly install_docs_template's cp (install.sh:1472),
4510:#                    so the destination inherits the template's bits.
4511:#   rendered route : shell redirection — exactly install.sh:1576's
4512:#                    `sed ... > "$dst"`, so the destination gets 0666 & ~umask.
4513:# MEASURED (S327): `cp` from the mktemp render buffer produces 0600 (mktemp is
4514:# created 0600 and POSIX cp copies the source's permission bits) while a fresh
4515:# install produces 0644 under the usual umask 022 — same bytes, different mode,
4516:# on the exact destination (.github/CODEOWNERS) the amendment exists to deliver.
4517:#
4518:# rail round-7 F3 — the write is ATOMIC: a same-directory temp file, the mode
4519:# set on THAT inode, then rename(2) over the destination. The pre-cure form
4520:# wrote INTO whatever inode already occupied the path, and an existing
4521:# destination hard-linked to a file outside the target shares that inode.
4522:# MEASURED pre-cure (S327), both mechanisms: `cp src dst` and `cat src > dst`
4523:# each changed the OUTSIDE file's bytes (sha before != sha after) and `chmod`
4524:# changed its mode — every symlink and ancestor confinement check passed,
4525:# because a hard link is not a link the path walk can see. `mv -f` replaces the
4526:# directory ENTRY instead, so the foreign inode keeps its bytes and its mode.
4527:# Same directory is a requirement, not a preference: rename(2) cannot cross
4528:# filesystems, so this temp file deliberately does NOT use _up_tmpbase (round 5
4529:# F3) — that function answers "where is SCRATCH?", and this is not scratch, it
4530:# is the destination being staged. It is removed on every failure path.
4531:# The mode has to be set EXPLICITLY here: `cp` onto the pre-created mktemp
4532:# inode keeps that inode's 0600 (measured), so relying on cp's mode-copy — the
4533:# round-3 F4 property — would silently ship 0600 and re-open MODE_DIFF.
4534:# _up_tpl_install_mode is the SAME function the normalisation path uses, so
4535:# "the mode a fresh install of this route produces" keeps exactly one owner.
4536:# rc 0 = delivered; rc 1 = nothing was written (caller reports and preserves).
4537:_up_tpl_write() {
4538:  _utw_src="$1"; _utw_dst="$2"; _utw_handle="${3:-}"
4539:  _utw_dir="$( dirname "$_utw_dst" )"
4540:  _utw_tmp="$( mktemp "$_utw_dir/.ceo-deliver.XXXXXX" 2>/dev/null || true )"
4541:  if [ -z "$_utw_tmp" ]; then
4542:    return 1
4543:  fi
4544:  if [ -n "$_utw_handle" ]; then
4545:    if ! cat "$_utw_src" > "$_utw_tmp" 2>/dev/null; then
4546:      rm -f "$_utw_tmp"
4547:      return 1
4548:    fi
4549:  else
4550:    if ! cp "$_utw_src" "$_utw_tmp" 2>/dev/null; then
4551:      rm -f "$_utw_tmp"
4552:      return 1
4553:    fi
4554:  fi
4555:  _utw_mode="$( _up_tpl_install_mode "$_utw_src" "$_utw_handle" )"
4556:  if [ -n "$_utw_mode" ]; then
4557:    chmod "$_utw_mode" "$_utw_tmp" 2>/dev/null || true
4558:  fi
4559:  if ! mv -f "$_utw_tmp" "$_utw_dst" 2>/dev/null; then
4560:    rm -f "$_utw_tmp"
4561:    return 1
4562:  fi
4563:  return 0
4564:}
4565:
4566:# --- rail round-7 F3: hard links are confinement holes the path walk misses -
4567:# _up_tpl_symlink_refuses and _up_tpl_confined_refuses both answer questions
4568:# about the PATH. A hard link is a second NAME for the same inode, invisible to
4569:# both: the destination is a regular file, physically inside $TARGET, and
4570:# writing it writes a file outside $TARGET. The atomic replace above already
4571:# makes the escape structurally impossible, so this is the named, auditable
4572:# refusal on top of it — an operator seeing `docs/rotation-log.md` silently
4573:# detached from its other link deserves to be told, not surprised.
4574:# Fail-OPEN when the link count cannot be read: that is INFRASTRUCTURE
4575:# (CLAUDE.md §4), and the structural wall (rename) is still standing.
4576:# GNU-first with the output VALIDATED, because on GNU `stat -f` SUCCEEDS
4577:# printing FILESYSTEM information rather than failing (the lesson
4578:# _up_tpl_stat_mode above already pays); `ls -ld` is the last resort.
4579:# PLAN-185 W1 — CONSUMER of the shared primitive. The body that used to live
4580:# here is now _wbm_nlink in scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh, so that ONE
4581:# implementation answers "how many names does this inode have?" for BOTH sides
4582:# of the delivery: install.sh refuses a hard-linked DESTINATION through
4583:# _wbm_dst_refuses, this side refuses one through _up_tpl_multilink_refuses.
4584:# Leaving the two copies to drift apart is the exact mechanism of PLAN-183
4585:# D1-D4 — six sessions of red main — and a hard link is the escape route no
4586:# path check can see, because a second name for one inode is not a link any
4587:# path walk encounters.
4588:#
4589:# An EMPTY answer means the infrastructure could not tell us, and the caller
4590:# does NOT refuse on it (fail-open on INFRASTRUCTURE, CLAUDE.md §4). A missing
4591:# library lands in that same branch, but it is also a broken checkout, so it
4592:# says so once rather than degrading in silence.
4593:_up_tpl_nlink() {
4594:  if ! command -v _wbm_nlink >/dev/null 2>&1; then
4595:    echo "    WARNING: hard-link detection unavailable (scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh not sourced) — destinations will not be checked for extra names" >&2
4596:    printf ''
4597:    return 0
4598:  fi
4599:  _wbm_nlink "$1"
4600:}
4601:
4602:# Returns 0 when the write must be REFUSED (same polarity as its two siblings).
4603:_up_tpl_multilink_refuses() {
4604:  _utm_rel="$1"
4605:  _utm_dst="$2"
4606:  [ -e "$_utm_dst" ] || return 1
4607:  _utm_n="$( _up_tpl_nlink "$_utm_dst" )"
4608:  [ -n "$_utm_n" ] || return 1
4609:  if [ "$_utm_n" -gt 1 ] 2>/dev/null; then
4610:    echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED $_utm_rel (destination has $_utm_n hard links — writing it would change every other name for the same inode, including names outside the target; break the link manually if that is intended)"
4611:    return 0
4612:  fi
4613:  return 1
4614:}
4615:
4616:# --- rail round-3 F4: MODE NORMALISATION ----------------------------------
4617:# `cat >` and `cp` onto an EXISTING destination both keep the DESTINATION
4618:# inode's mode; only a fresh create takes the install mode. MEASURED (S327):
4619:# `cp src dst` with dst pre-chmod'ed 0755 leaves 0755, while the same cp onto a
4620:# non-existent dst yields the source's 0644. So an upgrade refreshes the BYTES
4621:# and keeps a stale bit — and the parity classifier's MODE_DIFF, which reads
4622:# the exec bit (scripts/tests/_parity_classify.py:203), stays FATAL while the
4623:# upgrade reports success. The IDENTICAL branch never wrote at all, so it could
4624:# not converge either.
4625:#
4626:# "The mode a fresh install produces", per transform, mirroring install.sh's
4627:# own mechanism rather than a remembered constant:
4628:#   * identity — install_docs_template's `cp "$src" "$dst"` onto a
4629:#     non-existent destination (install.sh:1494) yields the SOURCE's mode;
4630:#   * rendered — the `sed ... > "$dst"` redirection (install.sh:1602) yields
4631:#     0666 & ~umask. The SOURCE cannot be consulted on this lane: it is the
4632:#     mktemp'd render buffer, mode 0600, which is exactly why _up_tpl_write
4633:#     uses `cat >` there instead of `cp`.
4634:_up_tpl_stat_mode() {
4635:  # GNU-first, BSD fallback, and the output is VALIDATED: on GNU `stat -f`
4636:  # SUCCEEDS printing the FILESYSTEM, not the mode, so "it exited 0" is not
4637:  # evidence that the answer means what we wanted.
4638:  _utsm_out="$( stat -c '%a' "$1" 2>/dev/null || stat -f '%Lp' "$1" 2>/dev/null || true )"
4639:  case "$_utsm_out" in
4640:    [0-7][0-7][0-7]|[0-7][0-7][0-7][0-7]) printf '%s\n' "$_utsm_out" ;;
4641:    *) printf '' ;;
4642:  esac
4643:}
4644:
4645:# $1=src_abs  $2=handle ("" => identity route).
4646:# The header stays a bare `name() {` on purpose: the oracles extract these
4647:# functions BY NAME with `sed -n "/^name() {$/,/^}$/p", so a trailing comment
4648:# on the definition line silently empties the fragment.
4649:_up_tpl_install_mode() {
4650:  if [ -n "${2:-}" ]; then
4651:    _utim_umask="$( umask 2>/dev/null || printf '022' )"
4652:    case "$_utim_umask" in
4653:      [0-7]*) printf '%03o\n' "$(( 0666 & ~0$_utim_umask ))" ;;
4654:      *)      printf '' ;;
4655:    esac
4656:  else
4657:    _up_tpl_stat_mode "$1"
4658:  fi
4659:}
4660:
4661:# Normalise the delivered destination to the mode a fresh install of THIS route
4662:# would produce. Silent when already correct; one named line per change, so the
4663:# convergence is auditable in the log. Fail-OPEN on an unreadable mode: a stat
4664:# that will not answer is INFRASTRUCTURE, not adversarial input (CLAUDE.md §4).
4665:# $1=rel $2=dst $3=src_abs $4=handle. Bare `name() {` header — see above.
4666:#
4667:# rail round-6 F4 — DRY-RUN PREVIEWS the same mutation instead of returning
4668:# early. Pre-cure, a destination holding the CURRENT framework bytes with a
4669:# drifted mode printed only `IDENTICAL` under --dry-run, while the identical
4670:# code path in a real run also chmod'ed and printed MODE-NORMALIZED. A preview
4671:# that reports LESS than the run it previews is not a preview; an operator uses
4672:# --dry-run precisely to decide whether to let the real run touch the file. The
4673:# modes are COMPUTED here (both lanes read the same stat/umask), so the line is
4674:# derived from this tree, never guessed — and the only thing skipped is the
4675:# chmod itself.
4676:_up_tpl_normalize_mode() {
4677:  _utnm_want="$( _up_tpl_install_mode "$3" "${4:-}" )"
4678:  _utnm_have="$( _up_tpl_stat_mode "$2" )"
4679:  if [ -z "$_utnm_want" ] || [ -z "$_utnm_have" ]; then
4680:    [ "${DRY_RUN:-0}" -eq 0 ] \
4681:      && echo "    NOTE: mode not normalised for $1 (stat/umask gave no usable answer)" >&2
4682:    return 0
4683:  fi
4684:  # Compare NUMERICALLY: 644 and 0644 are one mode spelled two ways.
4685:  if [ "$(( 0$_utnm_have ))" -eq "$(( 0$_utnm_want ))" ]; then
4686:    return 0
4687:  fi
4688:  if [ "${DRY_RUN:-0}" -ne 0 ]; then
4689:    echo "    (dry-run) would MODE-NORMALIZE ($_utnm_have -> $_utnm_want): $1"
4690:    return 0
4691:  fi
4692:  # rail round-7 F3 — chmod acts on the INODE, so a multi-link destination
4693:  # would carry the new mode to every other name for it, outside the target
4694:  # included. Defence in depth: _up_deliver_template refuses a multi-link
4695:  # destination before any branch reaches here, and after an atomic replace the
4696:  # destination is a FRESH inode with one link — so this fires only if a future
4697:  # caller reaches the normaliser by another route.
4698:  _utnm_n="$( _up_tpl_nlink "$2" )"
4699:  if [ -n "$_utnm_n" ] && [ "$_utnm_n" -gt 1 ] 2>/dev/null; then
4700:    echo "    NOTE: mode $_utnm_have kept for $1 (destination has $_utnm_n hard links — a chmod would change the mode of every other name for the same inode)" >&2
4701:    return 0
4702:  fi
4703:  if chmod "$_utnm_want" "$2" 2>/dev/null; then
4704:    echo "    MODE-NORMALIZED ($_utnm_have -> $_utnm_want): $1"
4705:  else
4706:    echo "    NOTE: mode $_utnm_have kept for $1 (chmod to $_utnm_want failed)" >&2
4707:  fi
4708:  return 0
4709:}
4710:
4711:# --- rail round-1 F2: PHYSICAL confinement, belt and braces ----------------
4712:# The reader already refuses a row whose dest or src is not a confined relpath
4713:# (_wbm_route_relpath_ok), so nothing hostile should ever reach here. This
4714:# assertion exists because "should" is not a property: the table is a FILE
4715:# (round 6 F3 removed the environment channel, it did not make the CONTENT
4716:# trusted) and this function is the LAST place before a write. MEASURED
4717:# pre-cure (S327): a row with `dest=../../outside/PWNED.md` put 536 real bytes
4718:# at "$TARGET/../../outside/PWNED.md".
4719:#
4720:# Two independent checks, both must pass:
4721:#   1. LEXICAL — the same predicate the reader uses, when it is reachable.
4722:#      A caller that somehow bypassed the reader still cannot pass `..`.
4723:#   2. PHYSICAL — resolve the deepest EXISTING ancestor of the destination with
4724:#      `cd -P`/`pwd -P` (bash 3.2: no realpath, no readlink -f on macOS) and
4725:#      require it to be $TARGET itself or a path UNDER it, comparing against
4726:#      the RESOLVED target so a symlinked target directory does not produce a
4727:#      spurious refusal. The parent may not exist yet on a fresh INSTALL, hence
4728:#      "deepest existing ancestor" rather than "the parent".
4729:# The check runs BEFORE `mkdir -p`, because mkdir -p of an escaping path
4730:# already creates directories outside the target.
4731:# Returns 0 when the write must be REFUSED (the polarity of
4732:# _up_tpl_symlink_refuses, deliberately: the two are read as a pair).
4733:_up_tpl_confined_refuses() {
4734:  _utc_rel="$1"
4735:  if command -v _wbm_route_relpath_ok >/dev/null 2>&1; then
4736:    if ! _wbm_route_relpath_ok "$_utc_rel"; then
4737:      echo "    ERROR: REFUSED $_utc_rel — not a confined relative path (route table poisoned?)" >&2
4738:      return 0
4739:    fi
4740:  else
4741:    case "$_utc_rel" in
4742:      ""|/*|./*|..|../*|*/../*|*/..|*//*|*\\*|*[[:space:]]*|*[[:cntrl:]]*)
4743:        echo "    ERROR: REFUSED $_utc_rel — not a confined relative path (route table poisoned?)" >&2
4744:        return 0 ;;
4745:    esac
4746:  fi
4747:  # rail round-5 F1 — CONFINED is not the same property as ALLOWED. A
4748:  # well-formed hostile table can declare `.git/hooks/pre-commit` (relative, no
4749:  # `..`, no glob) and every lexical gate agrees. The delivery DOMAIN is fixed
4750:  # in code, in the reader, and asked again HERE because this is the last stop
4751:  # before mkdir/cp — the same belt-and-braces posture the confinement check
4752:  # itself has. Fail-CLOSED when the authority is missing: in a real run the
4753:  # library is sourced (:106) and, without it, _wbm_route_dests is absent too,
4754:  # so the AC-9 precondition has already refused the whole delivery — reaching
4755:  # here without the predicate means a harness, not an upgrade.
4756:  if command -v _wbm_route_domain_ok >/dev/null 2>&1; then
4757:    if ! _wbm_route_domain_ok "$_utc_rel"; then
4758:      echo "    ERROR: REFUSED $_utc_rel — outside the delivery domain (this wave writes ONLY under docs/ or .github/)" >&2
4759:      return 0
4760:    fi
4761:  else
4762:    echo "    ERROR: REFUSED $_utc_rel — the delivery-domain predicate (_wbm_route_domain_ok) is unavailable; refusing rather than guessing" >&2
4763:    return 0
4764:  fi
4765:  # `|| true` is load-bearing: under `set -euo pipefail` a failing `cd -P` would
4766:  # abort the whole upgrade instead of reaching the named refusal below (rail r1
4767:  # follow-up, S327 — doctor.sh carries the same idiom).
4768:  _utc_tgt="$( cd -P "$TARGET" 2>/dev/null && pwd -P || true )"
4769:  if [ -z "$_utc_tgt" ]; then
4770:    echo "    ERROR: REFUSED $_utc_rel — the target directory does not resolve" >&2
4771:    return 0
4772:  fi
4773:  if _wbm_dst_non_directory_ancestor_refuses "$_utc_tgt" "$_utc_rel"; then
4774:    echo "    ERROR: REFUSED $_utc_rel — $_WBM_DST_REFUSE_WHY" >&2
4775:    return 0
4776:  fi
4777:  _utc_walk="$( dirname "$TARGET/$_utc_rel" )"
4778:  while [ -n "$_utc_walk" ] && [ ! -d "$_utc_walk" ]; do
4779:    _utc_next="$( dirname "$_utc_walk" )"
4780:    [ "$_utc_next" != "$_utc_walk" ] || break
4781:    _utc_walk="$_utc_next"
4782:  done
4783:  _utc_res="$( cd -P "$_utc_walk" 2>/dev/null && pwd -P || true )"
4784:  if [ -z "$_utc_res" ]; then
4785:    echo "    ERROR: REFUSED $_utc_rel — its nearest existing ancestor does not resolve" >&2
4786:    return 0
4787:  fi
4788:  case "$_utc_res" in
4789:    "$_utc_tgt"|"$_utc_tgt"/*) return 1 ;;
4790:  esac
4791:  echo "    ERROR: REFUSED $_utc_rel — resolves outside the target ($_utc_res is not under $_utc_tgt)" >&2
4792:  return 0
4793:}
4794:
4795:# --- rail round-7 F2: the SOURCE side of confinement ------------------------
4796:# The destination has been physically confined since round 1 F2. The source had
4797:# only the lexical predicate, and `[ -f ]`, `cp`, `cat` and sha256 all FOLLOW
4798:# links: a `templates/...` source that is a symlink (or has a symlinked
4799:# ancestor) to a regular file outside the checkout passed every gate and
4800:# delivered FOREIGN bytes into the adopter as framework content (measured
4801:# S327 — the delivered sha equalled the outside file's sha).
4802:# ONE implementation, in the library the three entrypoints share
4803:# (_wbm_source_confined), for the same reason ADR-194 gives the route reader:
4804:# a private copy is how the destination-side checks drifted apart in the first
4805:# place. Fail-CLOSED when the predicate is unavailable, exactly like the
4806:# delivery-domain check below it: in a real run the library is sourced (:106)
4807:# and without it the AC-9 precondition has already refused the whole delivery,
4808:# so arriving here without the predicate means a harness, not an upgrade.
4809:# Returns 0 when the read must be REFUSED (sibling polarity).
4810:_up_src_confined_refuses() {
4811:  _usc_rel="$1"
4812:  if ! command -v _wbm_source_confined >/dev/null 2>&1; then
4813:    echo "    ERROR: REFUSED source '$_usc_rel' — the source-confinement predicate (_wbm_source_confined) is unavailable; refusing rather than guessing" >&2
4814:    return 0
4815:  fi
4816:  if ! _wbm_source_confined "$SOURCE_DIR" "$_usc_rel"; then
4817:    echo "    ERROR: REFUSED source '$_usc_rel' — ${_WBM_SRC_CONFINE_WHY:-not confined to the source checkout}" >&2
4818:    return 0
4819:  fi
4820:  return 1
4821:}
4822:
4823:_up_tpl_register() {
4824:  # rail round-3 F1 — WHITELIST, mirroring install.sh:_append_delivered_template
4825:  # and the generator's own floor. Everything that reaches here today comes
4826:  # from _wbm_route_dests, so this refuses nothing in practice; it is the wall
4827:  # that keeps a FUTURE caller from registering a destination the shared table
4828:  # never declared. `command -v` guarded: the library is sourced conditionally
4829:  # (upgrade.sh:106, partial checkout).
4830:  if command -v _wbm_route_dest_declared >/dev/null 2>&1 \
4831:     && ! _wbm_route_dest_declared "$1"; then
4832:    echo "    ERROR: delivered-template registration REJECTED (not a destination declared in the shared route table): '$1'" >&2
4833:    return 0
4834:  fi
4835:  if [ -n "$_D1_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES" ]; then
4836:    _D1_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES="$_D1_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES
4837:$1"
4838:  else
4839:    _D1_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES="$1"
4840:  fi
4841:  if [ "$1" = ".github/CODEOWNERS" ]; then _D1_CODEOWNERS_REGISTERED=1; fi
4842:}
4843:
4844:# Deliver ONE destination. $1 = destination relpath, $2 = ABSOLUTE path to the
4845:# bytes to deliver (already rendered for a transform route), $3 = the source
4846:# relpath used to derive generations, $4 = validated handle or "" (render).
4847:_up_deliver_template() {
4848:  _udt_rel="$1"; _udt_src_abs="$2"; _udt_src_rel="$3"; _udt_handle="${4:-}"
4849:  _udt_dst="$TARGET/$_udt_rel"
4850:
4851:  if _path_is_skipped "$_udt_rel"; then
4852:    echo "    SKIPPED (--skip): $_udt_rel"
4853:    _UP_TPL_SKIPPED=$(( _UP_TPL_SKIPPED + 1 ))
4854:    return 0
4855:  fi
4856:  # rail round-1 F2 — LAST gate before anything touches the filesystem, and
4857:  # deliberately ahead of the `mkdir -p` further down (mkdir -p of an escaping
4858:  # destination already creates directories outside the target). Counted as
4859:  # PRESERVED for the same reason the symlink refusal is: nothing was written
4860:  # and the conservation law below still has to balance.
4861:  if _up_tpl_confined_refuses "$_udt_rel"; then
4862:    echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED $_udt_rel (refused — destination is not confined to the target)"
4863:    _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
4864:    return 0
4865:  fi
4866:  if [ -n "${_udt_src_rel:-}" ] && command -v _wbm_route_relpath_ok >/dev/null 2>&1 \
4867:     && ! _wbm_route_relpath_ok "$_udt_src_rel"; then
4868:    echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED $_udt_rel (refused — the route's SOURCE '$_udt_src_rel' is not a confined relative path)"
4869:    _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
4870:    return 0
4871:  fi
4872:  # rail round-7 F2 — PHYSICAL source confinement, before the `-f` test that
4873:  # would follow a symlink out of the checkout. On the rendered lane the bytes
4874:  # in $2 come from a temp buffer, but $3 still names the template this run
4875:  # read to produce them, so the check is correct on both lanes (the render
4876:  # site checks it FIRST, ahead of its own read; this is the second wall).
4877:  if [ -n "${_udt_src_rel:-}" ] && _up_src_confined_refuses "$_udt_src_rel"; then
4878:    echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED $_udt_rel (refused — the route's SOURCE is not confined to the framework checkout)"
4879:    _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
4880:    return 0
4881:  fi
4882:  if [ ! -f "$_udt_src_abs" ]; then
4883:    # rail round-2 F2: under --pin the DESTINATION list comes from this
4884:    # upgrader's own table (snapshotted before the checkout) while the SOURCES
4885:    # come from the PINNED tree — so a route the pin predates lands here. Say
4886:    # so BY NAME: "missing" and "not shipped at the ref you asked for" are
4887:    # different facts and an operator has to be able to tell them apart.
4888:    if [ -n "${PIN_REF:-}" ]; then
4889:      echo "    SKIPPED (source missing at pin $PIN_REF): $_udt_rel"
4890:    else
4891:      echo "    SKIP (source missing): $_udt_rel"
4892:    fi
4893:    _UP_TPL_SKIPPED=$(( _UP_TPL_SKIPPED + 1 ))
4894:    return 0
4895:  fi
4896:  if _up_tpl_symlink_refuses "$_udt_rel"; then
4897:    _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
4898:    return 0
4899:  fi
4900:  # rail round-7 F3 — a HARD link is a second name for the same inode and no
4901:  # path-based check can see it. Refused BEFORE the branch analysis, so it
4902:  # covers the INSTALL, REFRESH and IDENTICAL lanes at once (IDENTICAL still
4903:  # chmods through the normaliser).
4904:  if _up_tpl_multilink_refuses "$_udt_rel" "$_udt_dst"; then
4905:    _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
4906:    return 0
4907:  fi
4908:  if [ ! -e "$_udt_dst" ]; then
4909:    if [ "$DRY_RUN" -eq 1 ]; then
4910:      echo "    (dry-run) would INSTALL: $_udt_rel"
4911:    else
4912:      mkdir -p "$( dirname "$_udt_dst" )"
4913:      if ! _up_tpl_write "$_udt_src_abs" "$_udt_dst" "$_udt_handle"; then
4914:        echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED $_udt_rel (the atomic write could not be staged in $( dirname "$_udt_rel" ) — nothing was written)"
4915:        _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
4916:        return 0
4917:      fi
4918:      echo "    INSTALLED: $_udt_rel"
4919:    fi
4920:    _UP_TPL_INSTALLED=$(( _UP_TPL_INSTALLED + 1 ))
4921:    _up_tpl_register "$_udt_rel"
4922:    return 0
4923:  fi
4924:  # Ownership cannot be proven without a hasher => preserve loudly. Same
4925:  # posture, same wording, as _refresh_schema_doc.
4926:  if ! command -v _hash_file >/dev/null 2>&1; then
4927:    echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED $_udt_rel (no sha256 hasher available — ownership unprovable, not refreshing)"
4928:    _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
4929:    return 0
4930:  fi
4931:  _udt_h_dst="$( _hash_file "$_udt_dst" 2>/dev/null || true )"
4932:  _udt_h_src="$( _hash_file "$_udt_src_abs" 2>/dev/null || true )"
4933:  if [ -z "$_udt_h_dst" ] || [ -z "$_udt_h_src" ]; then
4934:    echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED $_udt_rel (hash unavailable — ownership unprovable, not refreshing)"
4935:    _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
4936:    return 0
4937:  fi
4938:  if [ "$_udt_h_dst" = "$_udt_h_src" ]; then
4939:    echo "    IDENTICAL: $_udt_rel"
4940:    # rail round-3 F4 — identical BYTES is not identical FILE. This branch
4941:    # writes nothing, so a destination whose mode drifted (or whose exec bit
4942:    # the framework changed between generations) could never converge: every
4943:    # future upgrade would find it identical and leave the parity classifier's
4944:    # fatal MODE_DIFF standing.
4945:    _up_tpl_normalize_mode "$_udt_rel" "$_udt_dst" "$_udt_src_abs" "$_udt_handle"
4946:    _UP_TPL_IDENTICAL=$(( _UP_TPL_IDENTICAL + 1 ))
4947:    _up_tpl_register "$_udt_rel"
4948:    return 0
4949:  fi
4950:  _udt_why=""
4951:  _udt_base="$( _baseline_lookup "$_udt_rel" 2>/dev/null || true )"
4952:  if [ -n "$_udt_base" ] && [ "$_udt_h_dst" = "$_udt_base" ]; then
4953:    _udt_why="recorded baseline digest"
4954:  else
4955:    while IFS= read -r _udt_gen; do
4956:      [ -n "$_udt_gen" ] || continue
4957:      if [ "$_udt_h_dst" = "$_udt_gen" ]; then
4958:        _udt_why="pristine prior generation"
4959:        break
4960:      fi
4961:    done <<UDTGEN
4962:$( _up_tpl_generations "$_udt_src_rel" "$_udt_handle" )
4963:UDTGEN
4964:  fi
4965:  if [ -n "$_udt_why" ]; then
4966:    if [ "$DRY_RUN" -eq 1 ]; then
4967:      echo "    (dry-run) would REFRESH ($_udt_why): $_udt_rel"
4968:      # rail round-6 F4 gave this lane a normalisation PREVIEW, because the
4969:      # write landed on an existing inode that kept its old bits and the real
4970:      # run then chmod'ed. rail round-7 F3 moved that responsibility INTO the
4971:      # write: the atomic replace stages a NEW inode and sets the fresh-install
4972:      # mode on it before the rename, so the real REFRESH performs no chmod and
4973:      # prints no MODE-NORMALIZED line (measured S327 on the H.16 fixture).
4974:      # A preview that announces a chmod the run does not perform is the same
4975:      # defect as round-6 F4 with the sign flipped, so this lane previews
4976:      # nothing about the mode — the mode it ends at is asserted by H.16.
4977:      :
4978:    else
4979:      mkdir -p "$BAK_DIR/$( dirname "$_udt_rel" )"
4980:      cp "$_udt_dst" "$BAK_DIR/$_udt_rel"
4981:      if ! _up_tpl_write "$_udt_src_abs" "$_udt_dst" "$_udt_handle"; then
4982:        echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED $_udt_rel (the atomic write could not be staged in $( dirname "$_udt_rel" ) — the file on disk is unchanged; a backup was taken)"
4983:        _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
4984:        return 0
4985:      fi
4986:      echo "    REFRESHED ($_udt_why): $_udt_rel"
4987:      # rail round-3 F4 — the write above landed on an EXISTING inode, which
4988:      # keeps its old mode. Converge to the fresh-install mode for this route.
4989:      _up_tpl_normalize_mode "$_udt_rel" "$_udt_dst" "$_udt_src_abs" "$_udt_handle"
4990:    fi
4991:    _UP_TPL_REFRESHED=$(( _UP_TPL_REFRESHED + 1 ))
4992:    _up_tpl_register "$_udt_rel"
4993:    return 0
4994:  fi
4995:  echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED adopter-modified $_udt_rel (matches neither the current framework generation nor any prior one — diff it manually; a pristine copy would have been refreshed)"
4996:  _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
4997:  return 0
4998:}
4999:
5000:if [ "$_TEMPLATE_DELIVERY" -ne 1 ]; then
5001:  echo "    SKIP: $_TEMPLATE_DELIVERY_SOURCE"
5002:else
5003:  # --- AC-9 precondition, asserted BEFORE any delivery ---------------------
5004:  # The route table is the only source of destinations. If it yields ZERO
5005:  # routes the loop below would deliver nothing and the summary would read
5006:  # `installed=0 refreshed=0 ...` — indistinguishable from "everything was
5007:  # already current". That is the vacuous pass this assertion exists to
5008:  # forbid: a count of 0 is a FAILURE, named, never a silent success.
5009:  # Fail-CLOSED because the table is INPUT, not infrastructure (CLAUDE.md §4).
5010:  _UP_TPL_DESTS=""
5011:  if command -v _wbm_route_dests >/dev/null 2>&1; then
5012:    # stderr is NOT suppressed: `_wbm_route_row_ok` emits the breadcrumb that
5013:    # NAMES a rejected row, and that breadcrumb is the whole reason round-1 F2
5014:    # is closed — a rejection nobody can see is the silence D3 was made of.
5015:    # It used to reach the log only because the registration fallback ~350
5016:    # lines below happened to re-run the same reader; rail round-4 F1 stopped
5017:    # that fallback from running on a failed precondition and the breadcrumb
5018:    # went with it (caught by H.13b). It belongs HERE, at the enumeration that
5019:    # decides, not as a side effect of an unrelated block.
5020:    _UP_TPL_DESTS="$( _wbm_route_dests || true )"
5021:  fi
5022:  _UP_TPL_ROUTES=0
5023:  while IFS= read -r _up_tpl_d; do
5024:    [ -n "$_up_tpl_d" ] || continue
5025:    _UP_TPL_ROUTES=$(( _UP_TPL_ROUTES + 1 ))
5026:  done <<UPTPLCOUNT
5027:$_UP_TPL_DESTS
5028:UPTPLCOUNT
5029:  # rail round-1 F2 — the DENOMINATOR. _wbm_route_dests now drops any row whose
5030:  # dest or src is not a confined relative path, so `routes < rows` is the
5031:  # observable signature of a poisoned table. Without this comparison the drop
5032:  # is INVISIBLE: the delivery would simply carry on with the surviving rows
5033:  # and report a plausible summary, which is the silent-continue the finding
5034:  # names. Counting stays inside the ONE reader (_wbm_route_rows_total) —
5035:  # a second parse here would be the second copy of the table CLAUDE.md §4
5036:  # forbids.
5037:  _UP_TPL_ROWS="$_UP_TPL_ROUTES"
5038:  if command -v _wbm_route_rows_total >/dev/null 2>&1; then
5039:    _UP_TPL_ROWS="$( _wbm_route_rows_total 2>/dev/null || echo "$_UP_TPL_ROUTES" )"
5040:  fi
5041:  case "$_UP_TPL_ROWS" in ''|*[!0-9]*) _UP_TPL_ROWS="$_UP_TPL_ROUTES" ;; esac
5042:  # Name the ORIGIN, never the tempfile: with the rail round-2 F2 snapshot in
5043:  # place _WBM_ROUTES_TSV points at /tmp, and a log line that named THAT would
5044:  # tell an operator nothing about which table decided this run.
5045:  _UP_TPL_TBL_SHOWN="${_UP_ROUTES_ORIGIN:-${_WBM_ROUTES_TSV:-<reader unavailable>}}"
5046:  [ -n "${_UP_ROUTES_SNAPSHOT:-}" ] && _UP_TPL_TBL_SHOWN="$_UP_TPL_TBL_SHOWN [snapshot taken before any --pin checkout]"
5047:  echo "    routes enumerated: $_UP_TPL_ROUTES of $_UP_TPL_ROWS table row(s) (source: $_UP_TPL_TBL_SHOWN)"
5048:fi
5049:
5050:if [ "$_TEMPLATE_DELIVERY" -eq 1 ] && [ "$_UP_TPL_ROUTES" -eq 0 ]; then
5051:  echo "    ERROR: the delivery-route table yielded ZERO routes — docs/ and" >&2
5052:  echo "           .github/ NOT delivered. A count of 0 is a FAILED" >&2
5053:  echo "           PRECONDITION, not 'nothing to do' (PLAN-183 W5 AC-9)." >&2
5054:  echo "           Expected scripts/delivery-routes.tsv next to the manifest" >&2
5055:  echo "           library, readable, with its dest/src/transform header." >&2
5056:  _UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_FAILED=1
5057:  _UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_REASON="zero-routes"
5058:  echo "    docs/.github delivery: routes=0 installed=0 refreshed=0 identical=0 preserved=0 skipped=0 precondition=FAILED — PRECONDITION FAILED"
5059:elif [ "$_TEMPLATE_DELIVERY" -eq 1 ] && [ "$_UP_TPL_ROUTES" -ne "$_UP_TPL_ROWS" ]; then
5060:  # rail round-1 F2: at least one row was REJECTED by the reader (escaping or
5061:  # otherwise malformed dest/src). Refuse the WHOLE delivery rather than
5062:  # proceeding with the survivors: a table someone can poison one row of is not
5063:  # a table this script gets to half-trust, and the rejected row's breadcrumb is
5064:  # already on stderr naming it.
5065:  echo "    ERROR: $_UP_TPL_ROWS route row(s) in the table but only $_UP_TPL_ROUTES passed" >&2
5066:  echo "           validation — at least one row declares a destination or source" >&2
5067:  echo "           that is not a confined relative path (see the REJECTED lines" >&2
5068:  echo "           above). docs/ and .github/ NOT delivered (fail-closed)." >&2
5069:  _UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_FAILED=1
5070:  _UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_REASON="rejected-route-row"
5071:  echo "    docs/.github delivery: routes=$_UP_TPL_ROUTES installed=0 refreshed=0 identical=0 preserved=0 skipped=0 precondition=FAILED — PRECONDITION FAILED (rejected route row)"
5072:elif [ "$_TEMPLATE_DELIVERY" -eq 1 ]; then
5073:  # Owner selection was resolved once before the destination preflight.
5074:  if [ -n "$_UP_GH_OWNER" ]; then
5075:    echo "    CODEOWNERS handle: @$_UP_GH_OWNER (recorded install request)"
5076:  elif [ "${REPLAY:-1}" -ne 1 ]; then
5077:    echo "    CODEOWNERS handle: NOT replayed (--no-replay) — the recorded install request is not consulted; the .template branch applies (install.sh parity)"
5078:  else
5079:    echo "    CODEOWNERS handle: none recorded — the .template branch applies (install.sh parity)"
5080:  fi
5081:
5082:  # Rendered CODEOWNERS bytes for THIS run, materialised once in a temp file.
5083:  # Rendering is what install.sh:1576 does; doing it here is what lets the
5084:  # rendered destination take part in the same ownership ladder as every
5085:  # verbatim one instead of being a special case with weaker evidence.
5086:  _UP_CO_RENDERED=""
5087:  _UP_CO_SRC_REL=""
5088:  _UP_CO_TRANSFORM=""
5089:  # rail round-2 F3 — the ONE transform this script can render, spelled out
5090:  # once. install.sh:1508 performs the same substitution; the table declares
5091:  # the value and this branch COMPARES against it. Anything else (empty,
5092:  # misspelled, or a future transformation nobody taught this renderer) is
5093:  # refused by name instead of being silently rendered as if it were this one.
5094:  _UP_CO_TRANSFORM_SUPPORTED="substitute:{{OWNER_HANDLE}}"
5095:
5096:  while IFS= read -r _up_dest; do
5097:    [ -n "$_up_dest" ] || continue
5098:    _up_src_rel=""
5099:    _up_rc=0
5100:    _up_src_rel="$( _wbm_route_src "$_up_dest" )" || _up_rc=$?
5101:    case "$_up_dest" in
5102:      .github/CODEOWNERS)
5103:        # --- rail round-2 F3: the ROW decides whether rendering is legal ----
5104:        # Pre-cure this branch dropped `_up_rc` on the floor, re-parsed the row
5105:        # with awk for its SOURCE only, and applied the OWNER_HANDLE
5106:        # substitution unconditionally — so a row whose transform was empty,
5107:        # misspelled, or changed to some future transformation still produced
5108:        # substituted bytes, contradicting the shared table it claims to obey.
5109:        # Read BOTH fields from the row and consult the reader's verdict:
5110:        #   rc=2 is the EXPECTED answer for a transform route (there are no
5111:        #        framework bytes on disk for it — that is why it has no
5112:        #        identity source);
5113:        #   rc=0 would mean the table declares `identity` for a destination
5114:        #        this branch RENDERS;
5115:        #   rc=1 would mean the row vanished between the enumeration and here.
5116:        # Only rc=2 AND the exact declared transform may render. Everything
5117:        # else is a NAMED refusal that writes nothing — fail-closed, because
5118:        # the table is INPUT (CLAUDE.md §4), not infrastructure.
5119:        # rail round-5 F4 — BOTH fields come from the ONE validated accessor.
5120:        # They used to come from two private `awk` calls over the same
5121:        # environment-overridable TSV: a FOURTH parser of the shared table,
5122:        # which ADR-194 vetoes by name, and one that inherited none of the
5123:        # reader's validators (round 1/3/5) nor its unterminated-final-row fix
5124:        # (round 4). _wbm_route_meta prints "<src><TAB><transform>" only for a
5125:        # row that PASSED validation; anything else leaves both fields empty
5126:        # and the named refusal below fires.
5127:        _UP_CO_META=""
5128:        _UP_CO_META_RC=0
5129:        if command -v _wbm_route_meta >/dev/null 2>&1; then
5130:          _UP_CO_META="$( _wbm_route_meta ".github/CODEOWNERS" )" || _UP_CO_META_RC=$?
5131:        else
5132:          _UP_CO_META_RC=1
5133:        fi
5134:        if [ "$_UP_CO_META_RC" -eq 0 ] && [ -n "$_UP_CO_META" ]; then
5135:          _UP_CO_TAB="$( printf '\t' )"
5136:          _UP_CO_SRC_REL="${_UP_CO_META%%"$_UP_CO_TAB"*}"
5137:          _UP_CO_TRANSFORM="${_UP_CO_META#*"$_UP_CO_TAB"}"
5138:        else
5139:          _UP_CO_SRC_REL=""
5140:          _UP_CO_TRANSFORM=""
5141:        fi
5142:        if [ "$_up_rc" -ne 2 ] || [ "$_UP_CO_TRANSFORM" != "$_UP_CO_TRANSFORM_SUPPORTED" ]; then
5143:          echo "    SKIPPED (unsupported transform '$_UP_CO_TRANSFORM'): .github/CODEOWNERS (this upgrader renders only '$_UP_CO_TRANSFORM_SUPPORTED'; route reader rc=$_up_rc) — nothing written" >&2
5144:          _UP_TPL_SKIPPED=$(( _UP_TPL_SKIPPED + 1 ))
5145:          _up_route_unrenderable
5146:          continue
5147:        fi
5148:        if [ -z "$_UP_CO_SRC_REL" ] \
5149:           || { command -v _wbm_route_relpath_ok >/dev/null 2>&1 \
5150:                && ! _wbm_route_relpath_ok "$_UP_CO_SRC_REL"; }; then
5151:          echo "    SKIPPED (unsupported transform '$_UP_CO_TRANSFORM'): .github/CODEOWNERS (the row declares no usable source: '$_UP_CO_SRC_REL') — nothing written" >&2
5152:          _UP_TPL_SKIPPED=$(( _UP_TPL_SKIPPED + 1 ))
5153:          _up_route_unrenderable
5154:          continue
5155:        fi
5156:        # MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE with .github/CODEOWNERS.template per run
5157:        # (install.sh:1551 elif vs :1563 else). Delivering both would leave a
5158:        # pair on disk that no install ever produces — §9.3 records that the
5159:        # two branches are not exclusive in TIME on the install side, and
5160:        # reproducing that here would widen a known defect.
5161:        if [ -z "$_UP_GH_OWNER" ]; then
5162:          # rail round-3 F5 — the SAME predicate the .template branch uses. If
5163:          # these two disagreed about what "present" means, the exclusivity
5164:          # invariant would hold only for the shapes both happened to see.
5165:          if _up_codeowners_present; then
5166:            echo "    PRESERVED (unclaimed): .github/CODEOWNERS (no recorded --github-owner — this run cannot reproduce the rendered bytes, so ownership is unprovable)"
5167:            _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
5168:          else
5169:            echo "    SKIPPED (branch not taken): .github/CODEOWNERS (no recorded --github-owner; the .template route applies)"
5170:            _UP_TPL_SKIPPED=$(( _UP_TPL_SKIPPED + 1 ))
5171:          fi
5172:          continue
5173:        fi
5174:        # rail round-7 F2 — the render below READS the template with `sed`,
5175:        # which follows symlinks, so the source has to be physically confined
5176:        # BEFORE the `-f` test (which follows them too). A refusal here writes
5177:        # nothing and counts as PRESERVED: the destination on disk is untouched
5178:        # and the conservation law still has to balance.
5179:        if _up_src_confined_refuses "$_UP_CO_SRC_REL"; then
5180:          echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED .github/CODEOWNERS (refused — the route's SOURCE is not confined to the framework checkout)"
5181:          _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
5182:          continue
5183:        fi
5184:        # The row was validated above; what is left is whether the PINNED tree
5185:        # actually ships those source bytes (rail round-2 F2 — under --pin the
5186:        # destination list is this upgrader's, the sources are the pin's).
5187:        if [ ! -f "$SOURCE_DIR/$_UP_CO_SRC_REL" ]; then
5188:          if [ -n "${PIN_REF:-}" ]; then
5189:            echo "    SKIPPED (source missing at pin $PIN_REF): .github/CODEOWNERS"
5190:          else
5191:            echo "    SKIP (source missing): .github/CODEOWNERS"
5192:          fi
5193:          _UP_TPL_SKIPPED=$(( _UP_TPL_SKIPPED + 1 ))
5194:          continue
5195:        fi
5196:        _UP_CO_RENDERED="$( mktemp "$( _up_tmpbase )/ceo-upgrade-codeowners.XXXXXX" 2>/dev/null || true )"
5197:        if [ -z "$_UP_CO_RENDERED" ] \
5198:           || ! sed "s/{{OWNER_HANDLE}}/$_UP_GH_OWNER/g" "$SOURCE_DIR/$_UP_CO_SRC_REL" > "$_UP_CO_RENDERED" 2>/dev/null; then
5199:          [ -n "$_UP_CO_RENDERED" ] && rm -f "$_UP_CO_RENDERED"
5200:          echo "    WARNING: PRESERVED .github/CODEOWNERS (could not render the template — not writing a partial file)"
5201:          _UP_TPL_PRESERVED=$(( _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + 1 ))
5202:          continue
5203:        fi
5204:        _up_deliver_template ".github/CODEOWNERS" "$_UP_CO_RENDERED" "$_UP_CO_SRC_REL" "$_UP_GH_OWNER"
5205:        rm -f "$_UP_CO_RENDERED"
5206:        ;;
5207:      .github/CODEOWNERS.template)
5208:        if [ -n "$_UP_GH_OWNER" ]; then
5209:          echo "    SKIPPED (branch not taken): .github/CODEOWNERS.template (a --github-owner is recorded; the rendered route applies)"
5210:          _UP_TPL_SKIPPED=$(( _UP_TPL_SKIPPED + 1 ))
5211:          continue
5212:        fi
5213:        # rail round-1 F5 — the two files are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE, and the
5214:        # `-n $_UP_GH_OWNER` test above does not cover the case that matters:
5215:        # a historical adopter whose install-state is gone but whose RENDERED
5216:        # .github/CODEOWNERS is still on disk. There the CODEOWNERS route
5217:        # resolves `PRESERVED (unclaimed)` — the file stays — and this route
5218:        # would then ALSO install .github/CODEOWNERS.template, leaving a pair
5219:        # on disk that NO install ever produces, permanently (the next upgrade
5220:        # finds the template IDENTICAL and never removes it).
5221:        # Presence of the rendered file is the whole condition: claimed or
5222:        # unclaimed, the adopter already has a CODEOWNERS and the template is
5223:        # the fallback for adopters who do not.
5224:        # rail round-3 F5 — presence via the ONE predicate, which also answers
5225:        # YES for a dangling symlink (`-e` alone answers NO, and the template
5226:        # was installed next to it).
5227:        if _up_codeowners_present; then
5228:          if [ -L "$TARGET/.github/CODEOWNERS" ]; then
5229:            echo "    SKIPPED (CODEOWNERS path present as symlink): .github/CODEOWNERS.template (a link — dangling or not — occupies the path; the two surfaces are mutually exclusive)"
5230:          else
5231:            echo "    SKIPPED (CODEOWNERS present): .github/CODEOWNERS.template (a rendered .github/CODEOWNERS is already on disk; the two are mutually exclusive)"
5232:          fi
5233:          _UP_TPL_SKIPPED=$(( _UP_TPL_SKIPPED + 1 ))
5234:          continue
5235:        fi
5236:        if [ "$_up_rc" -ne 0 ] || [ -z "$_up_src_rel" ]; then
5237:          echo "    SKIP (no identity route): $_up_dest" >&2
5238:          _UP_TPL_SKIPPED=$(( _UP_TPL_SKIPPED + 1 ))
5239:          _up_route_unrenderable
5240:          continue
5241:        fi
5242:        _up_deliver_template "$_up_dest" "$SOURCE_DIR/$_up_src_rel" "$_up_src_rel" ""
5243:        ;;
5244:      *)
5245:        if [ "$_up_rc" -ne 0 ] || [ -z "$_up_src_rel" ]; then
5246:          # rc=1 (no row) is impossible here — the destination came FROM the
5247:          # table. rc=2 means the row declares a transform this script has no
5248:          # renderer for: fail-CLOSED, named, never a silent skip.
5249:          echo "    SKIP (route declares a transform with no renderer, or the row is malformed): $_up_dest" >&2
5250:          _UP_TPL_SKIPPED=$(( _UP_TPL_SKIPPED + 1 ))
5251:          _up_route_unrenderable
5252:          continue
5253:        fi
5254:        _up_deliver_template "$_up_dest" "$SOURCE_DIR/$_up_src_rel" "$_up_src_rel" ""
5255:        ;;
5256:    esac
5257:  done <<UPTPLLOOP
5258:$_UP_TPL_DESTS
5259:UPTPLLOOP
5260:
5261:  _D1_DELIVERY_RAN=1
5262:  # --- conservation law ----------------------------------------------------
5263:  # Every enumerated route must have reached exactly one verdict. This is the
5264:  # assertion the route-count one cannot make: it catches a destination
5265:  # falling through a hole in the case analysis above, which would otherwise
5266:  # be invisible (no line printed, no counter moved, summary still plausible).
5267:  _UP_TPL_SEEN=$(( _UP_TPL_INSTALLED + _UP_TPL_REFRESHED + _UP_TPL_IDENTICAL \
5268:                   + _UP_TPL_PRESERVED + _UP_TPL_SKIPPED ))
5269:  if [ "$_UP_TPL_SEEN" -ne "$_UP_TPL_ROUTES" ]; then
5270:    echo "    ERROR: $_UP_TPL_ROUTES route(s) enumerated but $_UP_TPL_SEEN verdict(s) reached —" >&2
5271:    echo "           a destination fell through the delivery case analysis." >&2
5272:    echo "           Registering NOTHING from this run (fail-closed)." >&2
5273:    # Clear the LIST, never the RAN flag. Clearing the flag would hand the
5274:    # registration back to the D3 byte-compare fallback, which would happily
5275:    # register the very destinations this branch just refused to vouch for —
5276:    # a fail-OPEN dressed as a fail-closed. _D1_DELIVERY_RAN=1 keeps D1
5277:    # authoritative; an empty list is what "register nothing" means.
5278:    _D1_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES=""
5279:    _D1_CODEOWNERS_REGISTERED=0
5280:    # rail round-2 F2: same property as the two precondition branches — a
5281:    # named failure that exits 0 is a failure the caller cannot see. This one
5282:    # only fires on a real hole in the case analysis, so a red CI here is the
5283:    # correct outcome, never noise.
5284:    _UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_FAILED=1
5285:    _UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_REASON="unclassified-route"
5286:  fi
5287:  # rc.1 re-pass part 1 P1-4 — the two precondition branches above already
5288:  # carry `precondition=FAILED` on this line for log-only consumers; a
5289:  # per-route refusal has to say the same thing on the same surface, or a
5290:  # log reader sees a plausible summary while the run exits 3.
5291:  _UP_TPL_SUMMARY_TAIL=""
5292:  [ "${_UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_FAILED:-0}" -eq 1 ] \
5293:    && _UP_TPL_SUMMARY_TAIL=" precondition=FAILED — PRECONDITION FAILED (${_UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_REASON:-unspecified})"
5294:  echo "    docs/.github delivery: routes=$_UP_TPL_ROUTES installed=$_UP_TPL_INSTALLED refreshed=$_UP_TPL_REFRESHED identical=$_UP_TPL_IDENTICAL preserved=$_UP_TPL_PRESERVED skipped=$_UP_TPL_SKIPPED$_UP_TPL_SUMMARY_TAIL"
5295:fi
5296:
5297:# PLAN-161 U3 — mis-install scan/purge. Runs in ALL modes (flag-absent and
5298:# --dry-run runs emit the would-purge PREVIEW; deletion requires the explicit
5299:# --purge-misinstalled flag AND a non-dry run). Runs BEFORE the baseline-
5300:# manifest rewrite below so a purged path is never re-recorded.
5301:echo ""
5302:echo "==> Scanning excluded trees for mis-installed framework-internal files (PLAN-161 U3)"
5303:_purge_misinstalled_scan
5304:
5305:# PLAN-138 Wave C (ADR-155) C.7 — (re)write the baseline manifest AFTER a
5306:# successful upgrade, so a long-lived adopter who upgrades but never re-runs
5307:# install.sh (the S238 acme population) acquires/refreshes a manifest. The
5308:# NEXT upgrade then runs the manifest-present per-file classified path instead
5309:# of the fallback. Uses the SAME shared generator install.sh calls. Skipped on
5310:# --dry-run; fail-open (a generator problem emits a NOTE, never aborts).
5311:if [[ "$DRY_RUN" -eq 0 ]] && command -v _write_baseline_manifest >/dev/null 2>&1; then
5312:  echo ""
5313:  echo "==> (Re)writing install baseline manifest (.claude/.install-manifest.sha256)"
5314:  _up_record_op "rewrite_baseline_manifest" ".claude/.install-manifest.sha256"
5315:  export FMS_ROOT="$TARGET"            # enumerate what the target holds post-upgrade
5316:  export FMS_HASH_ROOT="$SOURCE_DIR"   # but record the FRAMEWORK hash, not the
5317:                                       # (possibly customized-and-preserved) target
5318:                                       # file — else the next upgrade clobbers it
5319:                                       # (C.5 idempotency fix). PROTOCOL.md pointer
5320:                                       # still hashes from FMS_ROOT inside the gen.
5321:  export FMS_PROFILE_PARTS="${PROFILE_PARTS[*]}"
5322:  # FMS_MODE mirrors the INSTALL's mode, not the upgrade's copy behavior
5323:  # (codex W1-ceremony round, P2): on a --mode link target the refresh
5324:  # branches preserve the symlinks, but a `copy`-mode rewrite would OMIT
5325:  # the SPEC/v1 directory-LINK record and hash the marker symlink as a
5326:  # file — doctor.sh then reports a type-change drift on a healthy tree.
5327:  # Evidence order: prior baseline LINK record (authoritative), else a
5328:  # symlink probe on the framework-owned roots, else copy.
5329:  FMS_MODE="copy"
5330:  if [[ -n "$_BASELINE_MANIFEST_FILE" && -f "$_BASELINE_MANIFEST_FILE" ]] \
5331:     && grep -Eq '^LINK  ' "$_BASELINE_MANIFEST_FILE" 2>/dev/null; then
5332:    FMS_MODE="link"
5333:    # Confine LINK serialization to the paths that ALREADY were LINK records
5334:    # (codex W1 round 10, P2). Without this, inferring link-mode from the
5335:    # prior manifest also promoted every OTHER live symlink — e.g. an
5336:    # adopter's own file under `.claude/hooks/` — into a framework delivery
5337:    # record. The probe branch below leaves FMS_LINK_PATHS unset (no baseline
5338:    # to derive from), keeping its pre-existing behaviour.
5339:    FMS_LINK_PATHS="$( awk '
5340:      {
5341:        idx = index($0, "  ");
5342:        if (idx == 0) next;
5343:        if (substr($0, 1, idx - 1) != "LINK") next;
5344:        rest = substr($0, idx + 2);
5345:        j = index(rest, "  ");
5346:        print (j == 0 ? rest : substr(rest, 1, j - 1));
5347:      }' "$_BASELINE_MANIFEST_FILE" 2>/dev/null || true )"
5348:    export FMS_LINK_PATHS
5349:    echo "    baseline rewrite: --mode link install detected (LINK records in prior manifest) — preserving LINK serialization for $( printf '%s\n' "$FMS_LINK_PATHS" | grep -c . || true ) recorded path(s)"
5350:  elif [[ -L "$TARGET/.claude/skills" || -L "$TARGET/SPEC/v1" || -L "$TARGET/.claude/.framework-version" ]]; then
5351:    FMS_MODE="link"
5352:    echo "    baseline rewrite: --mode link install detected (symlink probe) — preserving LINK serialization"
5353:  fi
5354:  export FMS_MODE
5355:  # Canonical PROTOCOL.md pointer hash (Codex R2 P0): record what the framework
5356:  # WOULD generate, never a preserved adopter customization. Empty if the
5357:  # pointer refresh did not run; the generator then falls back to hashing the
5358:  # target (install semantics).
5359:  export FMS_PROTOCOL_HASH="${_REFRESH_PROTOCOL_CANON_HASH:-}"
5360:  # PLAN-166 F3 (ADR-155-AMEND-1): conditional ownership from what THIS
5361:  # upgrade delivered/refreshed (or what the pre-upgrade baseline already
5362:  # recorded — ownership continuity), never the ceremony alone, never file
5363:  # presence (r17/r19/r20).
5364:  # The decision travels with the delivery flag.
5365:  export FMS_SOURCE_ROOT="$SOURCE_DIR"
5366:  export FMS_PRIOR_MANIFEST="${_BASELINE_MANIFEST_FILE:-}"
5367:  export FMS_HASH_SOURCE_SPEC="${_SPEC_HASH_SOURCE:-}"
5368:  export FMS_HASH_SOURCE_MARKER="${_MARKER_HASH_SOURCE:-}"
5369:  export FMS_HASH_SOURCE_PROTOCOL="${_PROTOCOL_HASH_SOURCE:-}"
5370:  export FMS_DELIVERED_SPEC="${_SPEC_DELIVERED:-0}"
5371:  export FMS_DELIVERED_PROTOCOL="${_PROTOCOL_DELIVERED:-0}"
5372:  # t8 P1: same delivery-record condition for the plans/ schema contracts.
5373:  export FMS_DELIVERED_PLAN_SCHEMA="${_SCHEMA_DELIVERED_PLAN:-0}"
5374:  export FMS_DELIVERED_DEBATE_SCHEMA="${_SCHEMA_DELIVERED_DEBATE:-0}"
5375:  export FMS_DELIVERED_MARKER="${_MARKER_DELIVERED:-0}"
5376:  # PLAN-183 W5 (D3) — docs/ + .github/ registration on the UPGRADE path.
5377:  #
5378:  # D1-HOOK: delivery of docs/ and .github/ on upgrade belongs HERE, above
5379:  # this block. upgrade.sh ships NEITHER tree today (measured S323:
5380:  # `grep -c github scripts/upgrade.sh` = 0; every `docs` hit is a comment) —
5381:  # that is defect D1 and it is what keeps the parity e2e at STALE 3. Until D1
5382:  # lands, this block only REGISTERS.
5383:  #
5384:  # The install precedent (install.sh:1318-1329, `wrote || cmp -s`) is a rule
5385:  # about a route the run PROCESSED; it is not a licence to claim a route the
5386:  # run never touched (rail round-4 F1, below). Ownership continuity for those
5387:  # is the PRIOR BASELINE RECORD — the same rule PROTOCOL.md already uses
5388:  # (HASH_PRIOR_RECORD, install.sh:2504), and the only evidence available for
5389:  # a RENDERED route (`.github/CODEOWNERS`, rc=2) whose delivered bytes exist
5390:  # in NO checkout. Registering them here is what makes the generator's lane
5391:  # choice OBSERVABLE instead of silently absent.
5392:  _UP_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES=""
5393:  # PLAN-183 W5 (D1) — when the delivery block above RAN, it is the authority:
5394:  # it knows the per-destination RESULT, which byte-compare can only
5395:  # approximate. INSTALLED/REFRESHED/IDENTICAL registered; PRESERVED/SKIPPED
5396:  # did not. Recomputing here would be a second copy of the ownership verdict
5397:  # and could disagree with the one that just decided the write.
5398:  #
5399:  # rail round-4 F1 — WHAT THE `else` MAY CLAIM, and why it is not byte-compare.
5400:  # The fallback used to register any route whose bytes happened to equal the
5401:  # framework source. On a run that delivered NOTHING that is not evidence of
5402:  # ownership, it is a COINCIDENCE: MEASURED pre-cure (S327), an
5403:  # `install --ceremony user` adopter who dropped a copy of the framework's
5404:  # `docs/BRANCH-PROTECTION.md` into its own tree came out of the next upgrade
5405:  # with that path in the framework manifest (`hits=1`, delivery line
5406:  # "DISABLED"), and `uninstall.sh:196` walks the manifest and DELETES on a
5407:  # SHA match — so the adopter's file was one `uninstall` from being removed by
5408:  # a framework that never wrote it.
5409:  #
5410:  # `install.sh:1318-1329` is not a precedent for this: its `|| cmp -s` runs
5411:  # INSIDE the delivery function, about a route that run processed. Byte-equal
5412:  # means "the framework's bytes are here" only once you already know the
5413:  # framework put them there. So:
5414:  #   delivery RAN      -> the per-destination verdict of THIS run (above).
5415:  #   delivery did NOT  -> the only admissible evidence is what a PREVIOUS run
5416:  #                        recorded: a prior baseline record for the relpath
5417:  #                        whose digest still matches the bytes on disk.
5418:  # One rule for both lanes (identity and rendered), which is also why the
5419:  # rc=2 special case is gone — the prior record was always the evidence, and
5420:  # the identity lane had no business using a weaker one. Under-claiming is
5421:  # the recoverable direction (CLAUDE.md §4): the NEXT delivering upgrade
5422:  # re-registers the path from a real verdict.
5423:  if [ "${_UP_DELIVERY_PRECONDITION_FAILED:-0}" -eq 1 ]; then
5424:    # rail round-4 F1 — a failed precondition means this run refused the WHOLE
5425:    # delivery because the route table could not be trusted (zero routes, a
5426:    # rejected row, or a destination that fell through the case analysis). The
5427:    # destination list below is READ FROM THAT TABLE, so registering anything
5428:    # derived from it is the same half-trust round-1 F2 refused at the write
5429:    # site. Empty, and the reason is already on stderr and in the summary line.
5430:    _UP_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES=""
5431:  elif [ "${_D1_DELIVERY_RAN:-0}" -eq 1 ]; then
5432:    _UP_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES="${_D1_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES:-}"
5433:  elif command -v _wbm_route_dests >/dev/null 2>&1 \
5434:     && command -v _wbm_prior_digest >/dev/null 2>&1 \
5435:     && command -v _hash_file >/dev/null 2>&1; then
5436:    # _wbm_prior_digest reads FMS_PRIOR_MANIFEST, exported just above. It is
5437:    # the library's own exact-relpath lookup — upgrade.sh used to carry a
5438:    # second awk for the same format, and one parser per format is the whole
5439:    # thesis of this wave.
5440:    while IFS= read -r _up_tpl_dest; do
5441:      [[ -n "$_up_tpl_dest" ]] || continue
5442:      _up_tpl_prior=""
5443:      _up_tpl_now=""
5444:      _up_tpl_prior="$( _wbm_prior_digest "$_up_tpl_dest" 2>/dev/null || true )"
5445:      [[ -n "$_up_tpl_prior" ]] || continue
5446:      # A regular file, never a symlink: a link is not bytes this framework
5447:      # left, and hashing through one claims whatever it points at (H.8/H.17).
5448:      [[ -f "$TARGET/$_up_tpl_dest" && ! -L "$TARGET/$_up_tpl_dest" ]] || continue
5449:      _up_tpl_now="$( _hash_file "$TARGET/$_up_tpl_dest" 2>/dev/null || true )"
5450:      [[ -n "$_up_tpl_now" && "$_up_tpl_now" = "$_up_tpl_prior" ]] || continue
5451:      if [[ -n "$_UP_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES" ]]; then
5452:        _UP_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES="$_UP_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES"$'\n'"$_up_tpl_dest"
5453:      else
5454:        _UP_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES="$_up_tpl_dest"
5455:      fi
5456:    done < <( _wbm_route_dests || true )
5457:  fi
5458:  export FMS_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES="$_UP_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES"
5459:  # PLAN-183 W5 (OQ-4, MIXED lane): the rendered destination rides the
5460:  # CONDITIONAL lane and must declare a hash_source or the generator
5461:  # fail-closes. On UPGRADE the only evidence is the prior record — upgrade.sh
5462:  # renders nothing today (D1). When D1 lands, a run that actually RENDERS the
5463:  # file must declare HASH_TARGET here instead, at the D1-HOOK above.
5464:  # Line-exact match: `.github/CODEOWNERS` is a prefix of the .template row.
5465:  _up_co_hit=0
5466:  while IFS= read -r _up_co_line; do
5467:    if [[ "$_up_co_line" = ".github/CODEOWNERS" ]]; then _up_co_hit=1; fi
5468:  done <<< "$_UP_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES"
5469:  if [[ "$_up_co_hit" -eq 1 ]]; then
5470:    # PLAN-183 W5 (D1): DECLARE ON EVERY DELIVERY PATH, never only on
5471:    # continuity — install.sh:2508-2511 records that the previous attempt at
5472:    # this wave regressed 24 cells precisely by leaving fresh deliveries
5473:    # undeclared. When the D1 block registered this destination it left the
5474:    # rendered bytes AT the target this run (INSTALLED/REFRESHED/IDENTICAL all
5475:    # end with target == rendered current source), so the target IS the
5476:    # delivered content => HASH_TARGET, the same shape install.sh uses for a
5477:    # fresh render. HASH_PRIOR_RECORD is the verdict on the non-delivering
5478:    # path, where (rail round-4 F1) the ONLY admissible evidence already IS a
5479:    # prior record with a matching digest — the declaration and the
5480:    # registration rule now name the same fact.
5481:    if [[ "${_D1_DELIVERY_RAN:-0}" -eq 1 && "${_D1_CODEOWNERS_REGISTERED:-0}" -eq 1 ]]; then
5482:      export FMS_HASH_SOURCE_CODEOWNERS="HASH_TARGET"
5483:    else
5484:      export FMS_HASH_SOURCE_CODEOWNERS="HASH_PRIOR_RECORD"
5485:    fi
5486:  fi
5487:  _write_baseline_manifest "$TARGET/.claude/.install-manifest.sha256"
5488:  unset FMS_ROOT FMS_HASH_ROOT FMS_PROFILE_PARTS FMS_MODE FMS_PROTOCOL_HASH FMS_LINK_PATHS
5489:  unset FMS_DELIVERED_SPEC FMS_DELIVERED_PROTOCOL FMS_DELIVERED_MARKER
5490:  unset FMS_DELIVERED_TEMPLATES FMS_HASH_SOURCE_CODEOWNERS
5491:fi
5492:
5493:# ===========================================================================
5494:# PLAN-153 Wave B item B2 — (re)write the install-state after a successful
5495:# upgrade, mirroring the ADR-155 decision-(iv) manifest rewrite above: a
5496:# pre-Wave-B adopter (no state file) ACQUIRES one on their first post-Wave-B
5497:# upgrade, so the NEXT upgrade can replay. Merge semantics preserve the
