   450	
   451	### Pin to a specific version
   452	
   453	```bash
   454	bash scripts/upgrade.sh --pin v1.11.2
   455	```
   456	
   457	The `--pin` mode:
   458	
   459	- Refuses to upgrade if `.claude/` has uncommitted changes.
   460	- Is **one-shot, not durable**. It checks the framework source out at
   461	  that ref, runs the upgrade, and restores the source branch on exit
   462	  (`scripts/upgrade.sh` `_upgrade_cleanup`). The ref is recorded in
   463	  `.claude/.install-state.json` under `last_upgrade.pin` as history
   464	  only: the next `upgrade.sh` replays `--profile` and `--stack` from
   465	  that file and **nothing else** (`scripts/upgrade.sh:817,822`). To stay
   466	  on a pinned version, pass `--pin <tag>` on every upgrade.
   467	- Has no MAJOR-boundary guard and no `--allow-major` flag — it
   468	  checks out exactly the tag you pass. Consult `CHANGELOG.md`
   469	  before crossing a MAJOR.
