   363	install-state and no banner. `--dry-run` returns before that failure but
   364	SHOWS the symptom: `would BACKUP + UPDATE` for a customized file where a
   365	healthy run shows `CONFLICT` — stop there; `mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/ceo.XXXXXX"`
   366	from the same shell is the test, `env -u TMPDIR` the fix.
   367	Two hook-side variables belong to the same check: launch Claude Code with
   368	`CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` ABSENT from the environment (`env -u CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`;
   369	never export it in a shell profile) — with no session id in a hook payload
   370	the compaction hooks fall back to that variable and can write and reinject
   371	ANOTHER session's plan (signed condition 78). And run the test suite with
   372	`CEO_STATE_ROOT` unset (`env -u CEO_STATE_ROOT python3 -m pytest ...`): the
   373	isolation layer does not neutralize it, and an exported value lets the
   374	compaction tests write real state outside the isolated tree (signed
   375	condition 79). Before `scripts/install.sh` and `scripts/upgrade.sh`, no
   376	`FMS_*` variable may be exported in your shell (`env | grep -c '^FMS_'` must
   377	print 0): the manifest generator reads them as inputs and the entrypoints
   378	initialize only the ones they set — `FMS_HASH_ROOT_PATHS` is never
   379	initialized by either, and `install.sh` never initializes `FMS_HASH_ROOT`.
   380	An inherited `FMS_HASH_ROOT_PATHS` makes the upgrade manifest record the
   381	TARGET's hash for a customized hook, which the next upgrade then overwrites
   382	as FRAMEWORK-CHANGED even under `--on-conflict=refuse`; an inherited
   383	`FMS_HASH_ROOT` makes a clean install record source hashes for rendered
   384	files (doctor then reports every one as DRIFT) (signed condition 81).
   385	If you export `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`, make it ABSOLUTE: a
   386	relative value is cached relative and, after a `chdir`, the invalidation
   387	flush writes the previous directory's journal under the NEW cwd (signed
   388	condition 24). And keep `.claude/state` a real directory holding only real
   389	files and directories — a symlink, FIFO or other object at
   390	`.gc-shard-cursor`, `context-pressure-last-bucket[.*]` or `.context-pressure-last-bucket.?*`
   391	(the GC strips one leading dot, then matches the dotted prefix, then deletes) is followed,
   392	replaced or blocks the hook (signed condition 28).
   393	
   394	The pre-v1.4.0 audit chain is likewise left in place (see `CHANGELOG.md`
   395	[1.4.0], «audit log resolves per PROJECT»).
   396	
   397	And run the upgrade with **no Claude session open** on the repository: a
   398	session started on v1.3.0 keeps its hooks resident, and two hook generations
   399	appending to the same audit log (only when `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH` is set)
   400	interleave their records — `verify_chain()` then reports a break that is
   401	an artefact of the mixed window, not tampering.
